{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 50, :comments ["<b>And Laban answered.</b> He was a wicked man, in that he spoke before his father. And furthermore his words testify to his evil character, that he put the bad before the good, in what he said: ״We cannot speak to you bad or good.\"" "<b>The matter has gone forth from HaShem.</b> That is, the events that happened to you are proof. And from here we learn that the matter of zivug is decreed from heaven — a matter about which our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: forty days before the formation of the child, a bat kol goes forth and says, 'The daughter of so-and-so is for so-and-so,' and even across the sea. And this is what Solomon, peace be upon him, mentioned (Proverbs 19): ״House and wealth are the inheritance of fathers, but from HaShem is a prudent wife.\" Scripture explained that which fathers bequeath to their sons — namely houses and money — but a prudent wife they have no power to bequeath to them, for she comes from HaShem. And he informed us by this that a prudent wife is more precious than house and wealth, in the manner of what is written (Proverbs 31): ״A woman of valor, who can find.\" And in the Midrash Tehillim it comes: come and see how powerful is the force of zivug, for we find that the Holy One, blessed be He, joined His name to zivug in three places: in the Torah, in the Prophets, and in the Writings. In the Torah, as it is said: ״From HaShem the matter has gone forth.\" In the Prophets, as it is said (Judges 14): ״And his father and mother did not know, for it was from HaShem.\" In the Writings, as it is said (Proverbs 19): ״And from HaShem, a prudent wife.\" And it is written (Proverbs 18): ״He who finds a wife finds good, and obtains favor from HaShem.\" And they further interpreted elsewhere that marriages are decreed from the hour of formation, as it is said (Isaiah 46): ״העמוסים מני בטן הנשואים מני רחם\" — and this is 'the daughter of so-and-so is for so-and-so, and even across the sea.'" "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'The daughter of so-and-so is for so-and-so, and even across the sea.' 'Daughter' — she is the yod; 'so-and-so' — he is the vav; 'for so-and-so' — he is the alef, which is 'across the sea,' and all is joined and unified. And therefore they did not say 'so-and-so marries so-and-so's daughter' or 'so-and-so's daughter is married to so-and-so,' for they wished to put the female first and to mention her father and her husband. And this is the expression ״גן בעדן מקדם\" — a garden in Eden from of old — and this planting was before the formation of the world, והמשכיל יבין."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:14:55.642618624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}